NNAAMMEE
       pamtoavs - convert a Netpbm image to an AVS X image


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppaammttooaavvss [_n_e_t_p_b_m_f_i_l_e]


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppaammttooaavvss  reads  a  Netpbm image as input and produces a Stardent AVS X
       image as output. AVS X images are one of the few image formats  Gnuplot
       ⟨http://www.gnuplot.info/⟩  v4.2 and later can use.

       _n_e_t_p_b_m_f_i_l_e is the input file, which defaults to Standard Input.  Output
       is always on Standard Output.

       Try the following:

           gnuplot> plot 'myimage.avs' binary filetype=avs with rgbimage


       See the GGnnuupplloott manual" (1) for more information.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       There are no command line options defined  specifically  for  ppaammttooaavvss,
       but it recognizes the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (See
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ .)


